/*
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * Rebalance the primary image area between TF-M (secure) and the application
 * (non-secure).
 *
 * The board default (zephyr/dts/vendor/nordic/nrf91xx_partition.dtsi) splits
 * the 448 KB primary image area (0x10000..0x80000) into a 256 KB secure slot
 * and a 192 KB non-secure slot:
 *
 *     slot0_s_partition  0x10000..0x50000  (256 KB)  <- TF-M uses ~130 KB
 *     slot0_ns_partition 0x50000..0x80000  (192 KB)  <- app overflows this
 *
 * Once GNSS location is enabled the non-secure image (OSCORE + Location +
 * nRF Cloud A-GNSS request plumbing + cJSON + mbedTLS) no longer fits in
 * 192 KB. TF-M's flash region is derived from slot0_s_partition, so moving the
 * secure/non-secure boundary down one 32 KB SPU region hands the extra 64 KB
 * to the application while leaving TF-M ~60 KB of headroom:
 *
 *     slot0_s_partition  0x10000..0x40000  (192 KB)
 *     slot0_ns_partition 0x40000..0x80000  (256 KB)
 *
 * Child reg values are relative to slot0_partition (base 0x10000). The 0x40000
 * boundary is 32 KB aligned, as the SPU requires. The unused secondary image
 * slot (slot1, 0x80000) and storage_partition are left untouched; re-enabling
 * FOTA later still has a full-size upgrade slot available.
 */

&slot0_s_partition {
	reg = <0x0 0x30000>;
};

&slot0_ns_partition {
	reg = <0x30000 0x40000>;
};
